{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AGZvBsaESKrjQAeKAzBTGZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Plan for #216\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\nChecked against the current tree: #215 has landed (`internal/config/load.go` accepts `route` on scanner overrides with `RoutePending`, `RouteNone`, `RouteNeedsHuman`), and `error-codes` is already in the starter set. The `scan` and `findings.jq` sketches in the issue's own \"Implementation plan\" section are the intended design (fail-closed checks, allowlist projection, golden fingerprints); the worker should treat them as a spec to verify, not as instructions, and re-run them against the tests below.\n\n1. New `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths`: comment lines plus `^\\.ard/[0-9]+/logs/`, `^vendor/`, `^node_modules/`. Reason: human-owned defaults. `testdata/` is not excluded.\n2. New `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq`: two stages selected by `--arg stage` (`project`, `merge`). `project` reads only `DetectorName`, `SourceMetadata.Data.Filesystem.{file,line}` and `Raw` (else `RawV2`, used only as the hash preimage), validates detector name `^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,64}$` and a clean repo-relative path, and emits `<base64 secret>\\t<json of d,f,l>`. `merge` groups by hash, takes the lowest detector and file, writes the fixed body (do-not-re-route sentence, six-step runbook, fingerprint, up to 50 locations), severity `high`, group `\"\"`, sorted by fingerprint. Body must keep keywords such as token/secret/password out of positions before `:` or `=`.\n3. New `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/scan` (mode 0755, POSIX sh): `set -eu`; find siblings from `$0`; exit 2 if `trufflehog`, `jq` or both `sha256sum` and `shasum` are missing; `mktemp -d` with an EXIT trap; always exclude `^\\.git(/|$)` plus `exclude-paths`; validate the optional `allow` file (`trufflehog:<16 hex>`, `#` comments), failing on a bad entry; run `trufflehog filesystem . --json --no-update --no-color --no-verification --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --concurrency=2 -x <file>`, piping through jq project (stderr to /dev/null) and a hash loop with preimage `ard-trufflehog-v1` NUL base64(secret), 16 hex chars; record every stage's exit status in files; fail closed on non-zero status, missing `finished scanning` summary, zero chunks on a non-empty tree, or result count differing from verified+unverified; print stdout only last. Never `set -x`; never use the forbidden flags (`--since-commit`, `--max-depth`, `--detector-timeout`, `--archive-timeout`, `--filter-unverified`, `--filter-entropy`, `--results`). Use `tab=$(printf '\\t')`.\n4. New `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile`: reuse cve's `GO_IMAGE` pin and jq checksums copied from `scanners/cve/Dockerfile`; add trufflehog version and per-arch sha256 args with `sha256sum -c`; `ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp`; no COPY of `scan` or `findings.jq`; header records the AGPL-3.0 licence and that the binary is not in the published image. The worker has no network, so the trufflehog checksums must be taken from the issue's plan text; flag in the PR that a human should re-verify them against the signed release checksums. Do not touch the root `Dockerfile`.\n5. `internal/roles/config.yaml`: add after the error-codes line a comment and `scanners/trufflehog: { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }`. This is the starter file under `internal/roles`, not `.ard/config.yaml`.\n6. `internal/roles/roles.go`: add `scanners/trufflehog` to the doc comment list (line 10).\n7. `internal/initcmd/body.go` (`initBody`): add a fixed note, in \"Before you merge\" or its own section, saying `scanners/trufflehog` is included, files leaked-credential issues for a human, needs a TruffleHog binary (AGPL-3.0, from its Dockerfile or the host), and how to opt out (delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/` and its override line in `.ard/config.yaml` before merging). This is a Go change outside tests; the issue's plan wrongly said none.\n8. `internal/roles/roles_test.go`: add the four trufflehog files to `TestFSContents` (line 32), the new `scan` to the exec-bit loop (line 46), and `TestEmbeddedTrufflehogRoleLoadsAsScanner` asserting `ScanPath`, `Every`, `MaxOpen`, `GroupSize`, `Autoclose`, `Timeout`, `Route == config.RouteNeedsHuman`, `Dockerfile`, and `Extra`.\n9. `internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`: add the four paths to `starterTree` (line 146), the trufflehog scan path and the opt-out note text to the PR-body strings (line 201), and assert the resolved trufflehog role has `RouteNeedsHuman`; assert `scan` is committed 0755.\n10. New `internal/roles/trufflehog_test.go` and `internal/roles/testdata/trufflehog/aggregate.want.jsonl`: tests below. Prefix new helpers with `th` to avoid clashing with `cve_test.go` helpers; reuse `needTools`, `mustAbs`, `decode`.\n11. `docs/proposal.md` (Scanners table row, a \"The trufflehog scanner\" paragraph covering flags, no verification, allowlist, fingerprint scheme and its unsalted hash, fail-closed rules, `exclude-paths`/`allow`, AGPL-3.0 licence and absence from the `ard` image, runbook, scanned SHA in `issue.md`; plus the init list and config example) and `CLAUDE.md` (add the role to the `internal/roles/` layout line). CLAUDE.md is a protected path.\n\n### Test plan\n\nCommand: `go test ./internal/roles/... ./internal/initcmd/... ./internal/config/...`, then `go vet ./...`. No network and no real trufflehog; a fake `trufflehog` sh script records argv and the `-x` file, and replays stdout, stderr and exit code from env-pointed files. Hermetic PATH of symlinked tools.\n- `TestTrufflehogFingerprintGolden`: `canary-raw-alpha` gives `trufflehog:d4bf4d1967fad7b7`, `canary-raw-beta` gives `trufflehog:ce658c895bb3b307`, also recomputed in Go; stable across detector, location, differing `RawV2`; empty `Raw` falls back to `RawV2`. Verify these golden values by running the script; if they differ, the script is wrong, not the golden.\n- `TestTrufflehogAggregates`: alpha by two detectors in two files (one duplicate location) plus beta; compare to `aggregate.want.jsonl`; 2 findings, files `[\"a.txt\",\"sub/b.txt\"]`, lowest detector title, severity `high`, group `\"\"`.\n- `TestTrufflehogDeterministic`: reversed and rotated input and a second run give byte-identical stdout.\n- `TestTrufflehogOutputPassesGuards`: `scanner.DecodeFindings` accepts output; `redact.Builtin()` finds nothing in title, body, fingerprint, files; 60 locations gives 50 listed plus \"and 10 more\"; backtick in path gets a longer fence.\n- `TestTrufflehogCanary`: unique markers in `Raw`-adjacent fields (`RawV2`, `Redacted`, `SecretParts`, `ExtraData`, `StructuredData`, `VerificationError`, `email`, `repository`, `repository_local_path`, `DetectorDescription`) appear nowhere in stdout, stderr or the temp dir; `complete` and `killed` (SIGKILL of the process group mid-stream) subtests.\n- `TestTrufflehogFailsClosed` (table): trufflehog exit 1 and 2, no summary, zero chunks on a non-empty repo, count mismatch, malformed line, non-object, absolute path, `..` path, `a/../b`, control character, `Data.Git` source, no Raw/RawV2, bad detector name, bad `allow` entry. Each: non-zero exit, empty stdout, expected stderr text, no canary in stderr, empty temp dir. Positive companions: empty repo with `chunks:0` gives empty stdout; `./a.txt` normalizes to `a.txt`.\n- `TestTrufflehogArgv`: exact recorded argv, none of the forbidden flags (also `--include-detectors`, `--exclude-detectors`, `--json-legacy`).\n- `TestTrufflehogExcludePaths`: shipped file gives `.git` plus three regexes; removing the file leaves `.git` only.\n- `TestTrufflehogAllow`: allowed fingerprint dropped with comments and blanks tolerated; missing `allow` keeps both; count check still passes.\n- `TestTrufflehogMissingTool`: no trufflehog, no jq, no hasher: exit 2, empty stdout, `<tool> not found`.\n- `TestTrufflehogBodyRunbook`: body has `Do not add` + `ard:pending` sentence and all six runbook steps.\n- `TestTrufflehogDockerfilePins`: `ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp`, `GO_IMAGE` equals cve's, trufflehog version arg, 64-hex checksums, `sha256sum -c`, no COPY of scan files.\n- Starter tests as in steps 8 and 9, and `ard config check` accepting the role. Avoid credential-shaped literals in committed test sources (the repo's diff guard); build fixtures with `json.Marshal`.\n- Edge: tree where all files are excluded fails closed (accepted).\n\n### Risk\n\nHigh-leaning medium. The code handles live secrets: a projection bug would publish a credential in a public issue, so a human must read `scan` and `findings.jq` line by line. Protected path touched: `CLAUDE.md` (merge waits for a human). Public interface: starter config and `ard init` PR body change for every adopter. Security-sensitive: secret only in pipes, never in argv, files, stdout or stderr. AGPL-3.0: nothing may be added to the root `Dockerfile` or the published image. Concurrency: kill and trap handling of the temp dir. Trufflehog checksums cannot be verified offline.\n\n### Size\n\nL (about 850 changed lines). Files: `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/{scan,findings.jq,Dockerfile,exclude-paths}` (new), `internal/roles/config.yaml`, `internal/roles/roles.go`, `internal/roles/roles_test.go`, `internal/roles/trufflehog_test.go` (new), `internal/roles/testdata/trufflehog/aggregate.want.jsonl` (new), `internal/initcmd/body.go`, `internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`, `docs/proposal.md`, `CLAUDE.md`. If over 1,000 lines, cut in this order: Dockerfile pin test, fold determinism into aggregation, move the killed subtest to #217, shorten the script header. Never cut the canary, fail-closed or argv tests.\ninternal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\ndocs_docker_integration_test.go\ndocs_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.go\nerrcodes_integration_test.go\nerrcodes_test.go\nlead_test.go\nlicense_review_integration_test.go\nlicense_review_test.g